  "uncertain": [
    "Board identity: image is titled 'Pimoroni Pico LiPo' and lists '4MB/16MB Flash'; it does not show a variant marking specific to the 16MB model.",
    "qwst-connector and debug-connector: label-to-pin mapping inferred from the printed label boxes sitting above each JST housing in left-to-right order; the image does not tie each label to an individual contact.",
    "qwst-connector and debug-connector: both connectors sit under the USB-C connector's horizontal span, so which end is 'closest to USB' is geometrically marginal (chosen by distance to the USB connector's center).",
    "Battery JST connector at the bottom is marked only with '+' and '-' polarity symbols; skipped as a battery-only connector, but it is unclear whether these symbols count as individual pin labels under rule 1."
  ],
  "notes": "Peripheral functions are printed as a peripheral-number digit plus pin name under column headers (UART, I2C, SPI, ADC; key: '0 SDA' = I2C0 SDA); recorded as e.g. 'SPI0 RX', 'I2C0 SDA', 'UART0 TX'. 'CONSOLE' is a dashed box enclosing UART0 TX/RX on pins 1-2. Board silkscreen numbers are added as the first function where visible; silkscreen for left pins 14-16 (GP10-GP12) and right pins 25-27 (GP19-GP21) is hidden behind the QW/ST/debug label boxes and omitted. '-' (GND) and '+' (3V3_OUT) silkscreen marks are symbols and omitted. Left-side 'PIO' and 'POWER' column headers are category tags and omitted. Pin 33 GND carries AGND in the ADC column."
